[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2596099608","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101640#issuecomment-2596099608","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101640","id":2596099608,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6avVYY","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-16T15:56:53Z","updated_at":"2025-01-16T15:56:53Z","body":"You are reading the raw depth buffer values which are non-linear due to being in clip space. You need to linearize the depth buffer before using it for anything. \n\nPlease take a look at our tutorial on post processing shaders, it explains how to work with the depth buffer quite well and gives you all the code you need https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/shaders/advanced_postprocessing.html#depth-texture\n\nTo be clear, it almost never makes sense to work with the raw value from the depth texture directly. You pretty much always need to convert it into another coordinate space before using it. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2596099608/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2596172505","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101640#issuecomment-2596172505","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101640","id":2596172505,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6avnLZ","user":{"login":"wgetJane","id":52103358,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTAzMzU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52103358?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wgetJane","html_url":"https://github.com/wgetJane","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wgetJane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wgetJane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wgetJane/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wgetJane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wgetJane/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wgetJane/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wgetJane/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wgetJane/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wgetJane/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-16T16:26:57Z","updated_at":"2025-01-16T16:26:57Z","body":"@clayjohn this is what the [example shader](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/shaders/advanced_postprocessing.html#example-shader) from that page looks like on my end:\n\nForward+\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2267498f-a481-4bcf-92f9-0aac9594bbaa)\n\nCompatibility\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0f19ed0f-1747-41d2-9153-af5daa5a0654)\n\nis there a screenshot of what it's supposed to look like (something might be wrong with my system) or is it supposed to look like this?\n\nif this is supposed to be what it looks like, then i propose adding a similar screenshot to that doc page for clarity","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2596172505/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2596392680","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101640#issuecomment-2596392680","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101640","id":2596392680,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6awc7o","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-16T18:12:45Z","updated_at":"2025-01-16T18:12:45Z","body":"That looks about right. Remember, shaders just do what you tell them to do. This one makes a gradient from black to white each meter as you move away from the camera. \n\nAs you learn how to write shaders its important to remember that:\n1. Everything is just math\n2. You are in full control of what you do with that math\n\nIf you want to do something silly like write depth directly to the final color value, you can do that if you want. The docs are not trying to teach you how to write a nice looking shader, the example shader is just there as an instructive tool to show you the elements that you need to know to work with depth values that come from the GPU. Whether it looks nice or not is beside the point","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2596392680/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2596451654","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101640#issuecomment-2596451654","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101640","id":2596451654,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6awrVG","user":{"login":"tetrapod00","id":145553014,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKz2dg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145553014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00","html_url":"https://github.com/tetrapod00","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/received_event