d_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wgetJane/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-16T18:44:40Z","updated_at":"2025-01-16T18:47:50Z","body":"> This one makes a gradient from black to white each meter as you move away from the camera.\n\noh that makes it a lot clearer, thanks, seems like my assumptions with working with depth was unsurprisingly wrong (my naive understanding of it was that it would just give me where the \"pixel\" is between my camera's near and far planes as a float between 0 to 1)\n\n> the comments on the page\n\nhuh are comments on the doc pages a relatively new addition? the comments on that page would've saved me a lot of trouble if i just thought to scroll to the very bottom lmao","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2596468155/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2596492393","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101640#issuecomment-2596492393","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101640","id":2596492393,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aw1Rp","user":{"login":"tetrapod00","id":145553014,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKz2dg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145553014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00","html_url":"https://github.com/tetrapod00","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-16T18:50:51Z","updated_at":"2025-01-16T18:50:51Z","body":"@wgetJane You might find this article useful for a general understanding of depth: https://www.cyanilux.com/tutorials/depth/, with visualizations. Do note that it's for Unity, so the details are *not* necessarily the same, but the general concepts should transfer. As far as I know, Godot doesn't have *named* concepts of \"eye depth\" and \"scene depth\", but it does have the concept of \"raw depth\" and \"linear depth\".","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2596492393/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]